Manage attached resources such as screenshots, docs, logs, and other files.

Use "task-board resource add" to create a new attached resource, "task-board
resource adopt" to register an orphaned local payload, "task-board resource
update" to replace an existing one, "task-board resource delete" to remove it,
and "task-board resource get" to materialize a resource back to the local
filesystem for inspection.

Usage:
  task-board resource [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Attach a new file resource to an element
  adopt       Register an existing unreferenced local resource payload
  delete      Delete a resource from an element (requires --confirm)
  get         Download a resource to the local filesystem
  update      Replace an existing file resource on an element

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for resource

Global Flags:
      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default ".task-board")
      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite
      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)
      --json                     Output in JSON format
      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check
      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)
      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)

Use "task-board resource [command] --help" for more information about a command.
