+# TASK-260715-24icoz — deterministic archive rework results
+
+Date: 2026-08-19
+Role: developer
+Disposition: ready for review under the accepted rework and acceptance-resume boundaries
+
+## Rework outcome
+
+- Added `archive-assets` to `scripts/relay_release.py`. It packages only the exact canonical four-target layout using a deterministic gzip stream and USTAR records.
+- The archive writer rejects extra files such as AppleDouble `._*` members and rejects source executables unless their mode is exactly `0755`.
+- Every tar member is a regular file with mode `0755`, uid/gid `0`, owner/group `root`, integer mtime `1784656987`, and no PAX headers. Stable target order is `darwin-amd64`, `darwin-arm64`, `linux-amd64`, then `linux-arm64`.
+- Added a regression test over the emitted tar stream. It asserts exact names/count/order/type/mode/ownership/mtime, empty PAX headers, sizes, hashes, absence/rejection of AppleDouble members, deterministic overwrite behavior, and rejection of non-`0755` source bytes.
+- Recreated and updated `TASK-260715-24icoz_portable-relay-assets.tar.gz` through `task-board resource update` from the four already-verified canonical executable bytes.
+
+## Retained archive contract
+
+Archive SHA-256: `1f0ba226ed591d1baf5f9464b33e45b7658a33bf5a1a114e77b6d22d3d9eef4e`
+
+Direct inspection of a fresh board download passed with exactly four regular members and no serialized AppleDouble, PAX, or xattr metadata:
+
+| Member | Bytes | SHA-256 |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| `darwin-amd64/relux-relay-darwin-amd64` | 2,623,664 | `783b94982e90f0ceed0af0fa11662d11a333e244b87256cbfa0f7d21695f3290` |
+| `darwin-arm64/relux-relay-darwin-arm64` | 2,487,362 | `8ac45b257099c9d2079b0bd2cb9ae489acfb86e443ba7ca7e4b4b2a56380d64c` |
+| `linux-amd64/relux-relay-linux-amd64` | 2,592,894 | `ddcb22ed4d4a978992a04096abae8adc58d0b8bf3bcdc0c0a006775797e2941f` |
+| `linux-arm64/relux-relay-linux-arm64` | 2,556,030 | `908b3d9ea3543b6144e2c99407c9aa02cc69e86c1cce80364d32dbdc3de8e0dc` |
+
+Measured executable total remains **10,259,950 bytes**, handed to `TASK-260715-1tzaed` for shipping-budget ratification. The measurement is evidence, not a new policy value.
+
+Direct retained-byte inspection with pinned Go 1.26.5 passed all four binary format, machine architecture, CPU baseline, minimum runtime, linkage, executable mode, stripped/no-DWARF, size, SHA-256, and report-privacy checks. Build identity remains relay `0.1.0`, protocol v1, source commit `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096`, release mode, `CGO_ENABLED=0`, Go internal linker, `-trimpath`, and `-s -w` with no external debug companions.
+
+## Runtime evidence
+
+Both accepted local baselines were rerun as unprivileged UID 502:
+
+| Target | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `darwin/arm64` native | Exit 0; canonical bounded identity and exact self-hash matched; protocol-v1 stdio returned the exact accepted 16-byte server hello; stderr empty; clean EOF exit. |
+| `darwin/amd64` via approved Rosetta 2 | Exit 0; canonical bounded identity and exact self-hash matched; protocol-v1 stdio returned the exact accepted 16-byte server hello; stderr empty; clean EOF exit. |
+| `linux/amd64` | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; not recorded as pass. |
+| `linux/arm64` | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; not recorded as pass. |
+| native Intel macOS | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; Rosetta evidence does not claim native-Intel execution. |
+
+## Validation and exit codes
+
+- Deterministic archive command and strict final archive contract: exit 0.
+- Fresh board-resource download, SHA comparison, exact member/hash/metadata inspection: exit 0.
+- Direct four-executable retained-byte inspection: exit 0.
+- Native arm64 identity + protocol-v1 stdio + clean exit: exit 0.
+- Approved Rosetta amd64 identity + protocol-v1 stdio + clean exit: exit 0.
+- Retained inspector using source commit `58676a23...` against current `HEAD`: exit 1 as required, `source commit does not match checkout HEAD`. Direct retained-byte inspection remained separate and did not turn this provenance mismatch into a pass.
+- `make relay-toolchain-test relay-shell-test relay-shell-vet`: exit 0; 34/34 release tests passed twice, all relay Go packages passed, and Go vet passed with pinned Go 1.26.5.
+- Standard-library trace coverage over affected inspection and archive functions: exit 0; 300/371 executable lines, **80.9%**.
+- Black, Python compilation, ShellCheck, Actionlint, and `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- Targeted artifact privacy scan for developer paths, private-key markers, and AWS access-key patterns: exit 0 with no matches.
+
+## Acceptance disposition
+
+The reviewer-requested archive defect is repaired without weakening source-revision or clean-checkout provenance. The retained tar stream is deterministic and contains exactly the four declared executable bytes with the required metadata. All original asset identity, linkage, size, debug-symbol, runtime, and deferred release-fixture evidence remains intact. No signing, VPN app/provider launch, NetworkExtension preference, route, or DNS operation was performed.
