+| `darwin-amd64/relux-relay-darwin-amd64` | 2,623,664 | `783b94982e90f0ceed0af0fa11662d11a333e244b87256cbfa0f7d21695f3290` |
+| `darwin-arm64/relux-relay-darwin-arm64` | 2,487,362 | `8ac45b257099c9d2079b0bd2cb9ae489acfb86e443ba7ca7e4b4b2a56380d64c` |
+| `linux-amd64/relux-relay-linux-amd64` | 2,592,894 | `ddcb22ed4d4a978992a04096abae8adc58d0b8bf3bcdc0c0a006775797e2941f` |
+| `linux-arm64/relux-relay-linux-arm64` | 2,556,030 | `908b3d9ea3543b6144e2c99407c9aa02cc69e86c1cce80364d32dbdc3de8e0dc` |
+
+Measured executable total remains **10,259,950 bytes**, handed to `TASK-260715-1tzaed` for shipping-budget ratification. The measurement is evidence, not a new policy value.
+
+Direct retained-byte inspection with pinned Go 1.26.5 passed all four binary format, machine architecture, CPU baseline, minimum runtime, linkage, executable mode, stripped/no-DWARF, size, SHA-256, and report-privacy checks. Build identity remains relay `0.1.0`, protocol v1, source commit `58676a23e2e0fb3fcc1b5005d59c6ed56d3c0096`, release mode, `CGO_ENABLED=0`, Go internal linker, `-trimpath`, and `-s -w` with no external debug companions.
+
+## Runtime evidence
+
+Both accepted local baselines were rerun as unprivileged UID 502:
+
+| Target | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `darwin/arm64` native | Exit 0; canonical bounded identity and exact self-hash matched; protocol-v1 stdio returned the exact accepted 16-byte server hello; stderr empty; clean EOF exit. |
+| `darwin/amd64` via approved Rosetta 2 | Exit 0; canonical bounded identity and exact self-hash matched; protocol-v1 stdio returned the exact accepted 16-byte server hello; stderr empty; clean EOF exit. |
+| `linux/amd64` | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; not recorded as pass. |
+| `linux/arm64` | Explicitly deferred to `TASK-260715-1c4l9v`; not recorded as pass. |
